{{Quote|[&hellip;] welcome to Coronet&hellip;the jewel of the Corellian system.|Wedge Antilles|<ref name="X-Wing: Rogue Leader 1">[[X-Wing: Rogue Leader 1|''X-Wing: Rogue Leader'' 1]]</ref>}}
'''Coronet City''', or '''Coronet''' for short, was the bustling [[Capital/Legends|capital]] of [[Corellia/Legends|Corellia]].<ref name="TCSWE" />

==Characteristics==
{{Quote|The most important planet in the Corellian star system in the Corellian Sector is Corellia, and the capital city is Coronet.|[[Han Solo/Legends|Han Solo]]|<ref name="AaC">''[[Ambush at Corellia]]''</ref>}}
[[File:CoronetCity.jpg|thumb|left|200px|A small portion of Coronet City during the Galactic Civil War]]
Often referred to as "'''The Jewel of Corellia'''," Coronet was a bustling urban metropolis located on the coast of the southernmost continent. It was a technologically advanced city with beautiful architecture, but its urban development paled in comparison to [[Coruscant/Legends|Coruscant]].

In keeping with [[Corellia/Legends|Corellia's]] spacefaring heritage, Coronet's spaceport was second to none. Coronet was also home to the headquarters of [[Corellian Security Force|CorSec]] and was heavily patrolled, although patrols were somewhat lighter in the [[Blue Sector/Legends|Blue Sector]], a rough section of town filled with cantinas, tattoo parlors, casinos, and fences, where offworlders tended to congregate.

The famous [[Treasure Ship Row/Legends|Treasure Ship Row]] was a large bazaar located just inside Blue Sector and was famous for offering just about anything a customer could desire, legal or otherwise. Underneath Coronet's maze-like city streets lay a vast underground [[Selonian Tunnels|series of tunnels and caverns]], where the [[Selonian/Legends|Selonian]] population lived and worked. Snaking its way among the Selonian caverns was [[Coronet Junction|the subway system]]. Similarly, the infamous [[Meatlumps|Meatlump Gang]] hid in the sewer system beneath the city streets. Here, they plotted a number of [[Terrorist/Legends|terrorist]] schemes against the populace.

The [[Corellian Space Museum]] was also located in Coronet City, filled with artifacts from the earliest history of space flight. The [[Corellian Stock Exchange]] was also located there.

The city also possessed a [[Hovertrain/Legends|mag-lev train]] system to transport cargo throughout the streets.<ref name="Star Wars: Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy">''[[Star Wars: Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy]]''</ref>

It was known for its parks and many open spaces.<ref name="TCSWE" />

==History==
{{Quote|A place without war. Never thought it possible.|[[Wes Janson/Legends|Wes Janson]]|<ref name="Star Wars: X-Wing Rogue Squadron: Family Ties">''[[Star Wars: X-Wing Rogue Squadron: Family Ties]]''</ref>}}
===Galactic Wars===
In [[3640 BBY]], Coronet City was the center of fighting on Corellia during the [[Battle of Corellia]], the first major battle of the [[Galactic War]]. The Corellian Council had quickly capitulated to the [[Sith Empire (Post–Great Hyperspace War)|reconstituted Sith Empire]] for power, and the Sith immediately moved to occupy Coronet City as a beachhead, and from there to take Corellia to the Empire. Coronet City became occupied by Sith forces, closing off all communications with the rest of Corellia and the Republic.

Later that year, Sith forces were driven from Coronet City and Corellia by Republic forces led by The [[Hero of Tython]] and General [[Var Suthra]] working with CorSec and resistance groups on Corellia, although there were millions of casualties in the battle and ensuing occupation.

===Rebellion era===
<div style="float:right">[[File:Coronet_City_from_Space_SOF.png|thumb|250px|Coronet City as seen from orbit]]</div>
{{Quote|Ahh, that was never my favorite building, anyway.| [[Han Solo/Legends|Han Solo]] after the capitol building was destroyed|<ref name="Star Wars: Rogue Squadron (video game)">[[Star Wars: Rogue Squadron (video game)|''Star Wars: Rogue Squadron'']]</ref>}}
In [[1 ABY/Legends|1 ABY]], [[Luke Skywalker/Legends|Luke Skywalker]] and [[Rogue Squadron/Legends|Rogue Squadron]] led an assault on the city, which was under [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Imperial]] occupation at the time. Their objective was to aid the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic/Legends|Rebellion]] in rescuing [[Crix Madine/Legends|Crix Madine]], a high-ranking officer in the Galactic Empire. At the same time, [[General/Legends|General]] [[Carlist Rieekan/Legends|Rieekan]], the commanding officer of Rogue Squadron, was attending a conference in one of Coronet's capital buildings.

Unfortunately for the Rebels, Imperial forces in the [[Corellian sector/Legends|Corellian sector]] had learned of both Crix Madine's defection and the meeting between the Rebel Alliance and [[Corellian/Legends|Corellian]] officials&mdash;this presented Rogue Squadron with a dilemma: protect an important member of the Rebellion, or rescue an equally important asset of the Empire. The team frantically raced between both objectives, which were under fierce bombardment from [[TIE/sa tactical bomber/Legends|TIE/sa bomber]] squadrons and [[All Terrain Armored Transport/Legends|AT-AT]] assault, but it seemed that both of the officials were doomed.

When defeat looked at hand, [[Han Solo/Legends|Han Solo]] and his [[Wookiee/Legends|Wookiee]] co-pilot [[Chewbacca/Legends|Chewbacca]] arrived in the [[Millennium Falcon/Legends|''Millennium Falcon'']], and provided the Rogues with much needed support. They used their space freighter to evacuate those trapped in the capital building, allowing [[Commander/Legends|Commander]] Luke Skywalker to concentrate on aiding the rescue of Crix Madine, who by this point had become locked down in the Coronet tech center&mdash;the arranged pick up point for the Imperial traitor.

[[File:Corellia_2.jpg|thumb|left|200px|The capitol building which was destroyed in [[1 ABY/Legends|1 ABY]] by the [[Galactic Empire/Legends|Empire]].]]
Moments before the meeting place of Corellian and Alliance delegates crumbled under successive bombing runs from Imperial fighters, the ''Millennium Falcon'' was able to take off from the rooftop of the doomed structure, while the Rogues held off the advancing Imperial forces nearing the tech center. Soon, two [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter/Legends|TIE Fighter]] groups, both coming from opposite directions, attempted to intercept an incoming shuttle but failed as Rogue Squadron held off the two waves, securing the successful escape of their defecting officer. As Crix Madine fled the planet, Rogue Squadron rendezvoused with the Rebel [[Lambda-class T-4a shuttle/Legends|evacuation shuttle]] and the ''Millennium Falcon'', just as two modified TIE Bombers released their payload on the structure.

During the [[Disciples of Ragnos]] crisis, the [[Jedi/Legends|Jedi]] of Skywalker's [[Jedi Praxeum]] had information that the Corellians had reports of the cult's activity. [[Kyle Katarn]] and [[Jaden Korr]] [[Mission to Corellia (Disciples of Ragnos crisis)|went]] to investigate, and soon discovered that the cult members had hijacked a beam tram, and had also armed a bomb. Jaden fought his way forward from the back of the tram and disarmed the bomb, while Kyle used his ship, the ''[[Raven's Claw]]'', to destroy the [[Hover Transport TC9]]s that had dropped the cultists off on the tram. With the bomb disarmed, the cultists sped up the tram in an attempt to ram it into the station, but Jaden was able to make it to the control car at the front of the tram and stop it before it crashed.<ref name="Star Wars: Jedi Knight: Jedi Academy" />

During the early [[Yuuzhan Vong War]] it was the site of large-scale rioting after the [[New Republic Advisory Council]] voted to redirect a fleet from [[Corellia/Legends|Corellia]] to [[Bothawui/Legends|Bothawui]].

The capital city of the planet [[Trigalis/Legends|Trigalis]], [[New Coronet]], was presumably named after Coronet City.

